{
  "type": "encoder",
  "name": "Rotary encoder",
  "category": "Motors & motion",
  "prefix": "SW",
  "description": "Incremental rotary encoder like an EC11 or KY-040: contacts A and B close to C in quadrature, one cycle per detent (A before B turning clockwise), both open at rest; 20 detents per turn. Turn it while running by dragging it or with the wheel (one detent per step); pull-ups on A and B (or the board's) give the pulses. For the push switch place a push button",
